---
description: Investigates and triages a CoreWeave baremetal node / BMN (by serial, bmn, deviceslot, bmc_ip, or k8s node name) — resolves identity, pulls FLCC/NLCC state, alerts, conditions, HPC-verification, IB, kernel logs, SEL, and actor attribution, correlates against Jira/Confluence runbooks and Slack known-issue threads via Glean, then returns a formatted disposition with key findings and ranked resolution steps and records it to Engram memory under topic_key node/<bmn> so repeat offenders and known signatures accumulate. Use for "why did node X fail", fail@node-zap, fail@fielddiag, CW0124, CW0002, MODS codes, GPU fell off the bus, SError, bmaas-power-cycle loops, return-to-fleet, repeat offenders, and RMA-or-retry decisions. Not for cluster-wide or rack-bringup program status.
mode: subagent
model: anthropic/claude-opus-5
variant: high
color: error
permission:
  edit: deny
  read: allow
  grep: allow
  glob: allow
  list: allow
  # Needs `explore` for 260KB AWX log parsing (see Phase notes), and nothing
  # else. Blanket allow would let this read-only agent spawn the built-in
  # `general` agent, which has full write access, defeating `edit: deny`.
  # Last matching rule wins, so "*" must stay first.
  task:
    "*": "deny"
    "explore": "allow"
  todowrite: allow
  question: deny
  # Node log bundles + rack summaries live outside the workspace root.
  external_directory:
    "*": "deny"
    "~/nodes/**": "allow"
    "/tmp/**": "allow"
    "/var/folders/**": "allow"
  # Read-only shell. Last matching pattern wins, so "*" stays first.
  bash:
    "*": "deny"
    "ls*": "allow"
    "pwd": "allow"
    "cat*": "allow"
    "head*": "allow"
    "tail*": "allow"
    "wc*": "allow"
    "file*": "allow"
    "tar -tf*": "allow"
    "tar -tzf*": "allow"
---

